scored tokens: ' Great Gatsby" is a novel by F. Scott Fitzgerald that captures the essence of the Jazz Age, a period in the 1920s marked by prosperity, excess, and the pursuit of the American Dream. Set in the summer of 1922 on Long Island\'s North Shore, the story is narrated by Nick Carraway, a Yale graduate who moves to West Egg to learn the bond business. He lives next door to the mysterious and wealthy Jay Gatsby, who is known for his extravagant parties. Gatsby\'s obsession with the past and his unrequited love for Daisy Buchanan, Nick\'s cousin and Tom Buchanan\'s wife, drive the narrative. The novel explores themes of wealth, class, love, and the illusion versus reality of the American Dream. As Gatsby\'s grandiose facade crumbles, the story culminates in tragedy, leaving the reader to ponder the hollowness of the pursuit of material success and the corrupting influence of wealth on the American Dream.<|endoftext|>'
